           PaneBox[
            
            StyleBox["\<\"MBEvaluate[MBInt, {Eps, Ord}] returns the expansion \
of the Mellin-Barnes integral MBInt in Eps, from its leading pole through the \
order Eps^Ord, in terms of multiple polylogarithms G, Log, Zeta and \
Pi.\\n\\nMBInt  - the MB integrand, built from Gamma and PolyGamma functions \
and powers of the kinematic variables\\nEps    - the dimensional regulator \
appearing in MBInt\\nOrd    - the deepest order of Eps to be \
evaluated\\n\\nThe integration variables are the variables inside the Gamma \
and PolyGamma functions and the kinematic variables are whatever is left, so \
neither has to be given. MBEvaluate[MBInt, MBVar, {Eps, Ord}] names the \
kinematic variables explicitly; they are taken in 0 < x < 1.\\n\\nA \
coefficient that could not be brought to a closed form is returned as \
MBFailed[reasons].\\n\\nOptions:\\n  Method -> Automatic       tries the \
methods available on this machine in the order \\\"SymbolicSum\\\", \
\\\"ExpandInt\\\", \\\"Subtraction\\\", each one only on the orders the \
earlier ones left open; \\\"SymbolicSum\\\", \\\"ExpandInt\\\" or \
\\\"Subtraction\\\" uses that method alone (\\\"HyperLog\\\" and \\\"Standard\
\\\" are accepted as aliases of \\\"ExpandInt\\\", and \\\"Resum\\\" of \
\\\"SymbolicSum\\\")\\n  Verbose -> False          prints one line per \
stage\\n  BarnesReduce -> True      applies the Barnes lemmas before the \
SymbolicSum method solves the integral\\n  Complex -> False          returns \
the real part; True returns the full complex value\\n\\nExamples:\\n  \
MBEvaluate[MB1, {\[Epsilon], 0}]\\n  MBEvaluate[MB1, {\[Epsilon], 0}, Method \
-> \\\"ExpandInt\\\"]\\n  MBEvaluate[MB1u, {\[Epsilon], -1}, Complex -> True]\
\"\>", "InformationUsageText",
